a grim scene that has come to represent  a country in grip of a major health  crisis  the fires at cremation grounds are  constantly burning  as bodies of those who've died from  covet 19 keep coming  this one in uttar pradesh one of the  state's worst hit by india's second wave  we used to get up to 10 bodies a day now  it has risen to 40 or 50 a day  nationwide the number of new cases has  exceeded 400  000 for four consecutive days bringing  the total number of confirmed infections  at over 22 million about 15 percent of  the cases worldwide  some say those numbers are undercounted  hospitals have been unable to cope with  the crisis a lack of oxygen and beds  continues to [ __ ]  the health care system that's making it  difficult  for many people to get much-needed care  prayam couldn't get treatment in his  hometown  so sick as he is made his way to the  capital new delhi  i really know about the status of the  hospitals of the faridabad you know  directly approach it here and luckily  fortunately i just got  the bed on one shot the government has  recruited  hundreds of former army medics to help  but it's coming under intense public  criticism  for its handling of the situation so far  many wondering why a countrywide  lockdown has not been imposed  like in the early stages of the pandemic  leaving local governments  to impose their own restrictions new  delhi has announced its lockdown will be  extended for a second time  now to may 17th the metro service has  been suspended  and people are only allowed outdoors for  basic necessities  kalakar decided to return home a  thousand kilometers away from the  capital  private company i work for a financial  company that is now shut down because of  the pandemic  i have no choice but to go back to my  village here the situation is very bad  we will be safer there that's the main  reason we're going back  india is the world's leading producer of  coronavirus vaccines  yet most people are unable to get a shot  prime minister narendra modi is also  under pressure to deregulate production  so more doses can be made available in  the country  even though some experts say they can  soon become  ineffective against the indian variant  of covet 19.  hamid al-jazeera
 

